{#
    A module's public page (module-interface `Screens::public()`, ADR-0059) in the theme's shell: menus, skip link,
    language links and footer come from the theme; the module's template draws the main content, starting with its
    <h1>. `head` holds the description, canonical and alternate links and JSON-LD built from the page's SeoEntry.
    Context: what ModuleScreens gives (`title`, `module_template`, `module_context`, `head` …).
#}
{% extends 'master.html.twig' %}
{% block title %}{{ title }}{% endblock %}
{% block main %}
<div class="container module-screen">
    {% include module_template with module_context only %}
</div>
{% endblock %}
